255:- `artifact-approval-<uuid>.json`: exactly `format` (integer 1), `kind` (`artifact_approval`), `id`, `reviewer_id` (canonical UUID), `approved_utc` (UTC), `decision` (`approved`), `manifest_hash`, and `revision_hash`. Approval must precede authorization issuance and match the independently reviewed artifacts. The repository manifest remains `pending_independent_review`; a future independent approval is a separate evidence record, never a change inferred from digest matching.
265:Run the dedicated website `.venv` interpreter with `PYTEST_DISABLE_PLUGIN_AUTOLOAD=1`, empty `PYTEST_ADDOPTS`/`PYTEST_PLUGINS`, repository plus tests on `PYTHONPATH`, and `-B -m pytest -p migration_offline -q`. Explicitly select all eight test files: `tests/test_database_config.py`, `tests/test_migration_config.py`, `tests/test_migration_artifacts.py`, `tests/test_migration_authorization.py`, `tests/test_migration_catalog.py`, `tests/test_migration_runner.py`, `tests/test_migration_provenance.py`, and `tests/test_migration_operational.py`. The plugin blocks credential/network/database access before collection, guards real BootstrapAudit file reads, and redirects operational file tests to temporary directories. Approval and authorization records in tests are synthetic. No live Alembic operation or real owner issuance is part of these checks.
687:The GraManna admin dashboard must clearly identify the environment from which statistics are being retrieved.
923:| `notification_release_events` | PK `event_id`; `source_approval_id`, `environment`, `platform`, `release_id`, `release_url`, `approved_at`, `audience_cutoff`, fixed `content_version`, canonical `payload_digest`, `status`, `created_at`, `updated_at`; UNIQUE `(environment, platform)` forbids a second semantic launch announcement even under another event ID. |
